-- title:
--   Lifting a bialgebra map along a unipotent finite flat Hopf algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain, $p$ a prime number such that $p$ is irreducible in $O$ (a uniformiser), and $k$ a field equipped with an $O$-algebra structure whose structure map $O \to k$ is surjective with kernel the ideal generated by $p$; thus $k$ is the residue field $O/pO$. Let $\mathcal R$ be a commutative $O$-bialgebra which is finite and free as an $O$-module, and let $H$ be a commutative $O$-Hopf algebra which is cocommutative and finite free over $O$, with $\operatorname{finrank}_O H = p^a$ for some natural number $a$. Assume the unipotence hypothesis that [`CartierDual k (TensorProduct O k H)`](def/HopfAlgebra_CartierDual.html#L12), the $k$-linear dual $\operatorname{Hom}_k(k \otimes_O H, k)$ of the special fibre with its ring structure, is a local ring. Let $\psi \colon k \otimes_O H \to k \otimes_O \mathcal R$ be a homomorphism of $k$-bialgebras, and let $x \colon H \to \mathcal R$ be a homomorphism of $O$-algebras whose base change $\mathrm{id}_k \otimes x$ coincides with the underlying $k$-algebra homomorphism of $\psi$. Then there exists a homomorphism of $O$-bialgebras $\Phi \colon H \to \mathcal R$ whose underlying $O$-algebra homomorphism is $x$; that is, $x$ is automatically compatible with the comultiplications and counits.
--
--   This is Fontaine's "first step": dually, a morphism of $O$-schemes from $\operatorname{Spec} \mathcal R$ to the finite flat unipotent $p$-group $\operatorname{Spec} H$ whose special fibre is a homomorphism of group schemes is itself a homomorphism of group schemes. It rests on the rigidity statement [`HopfAlgebra.algHom_eq_of_forall_sub_mem_span_of_isLocalRing_cartierDual`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.algHom_eq_of_forall_sub_mem_span_of_isLocalRing_cartierDual) (two $O$-algebra maps out of $H$ into a finite free $O$-algebra agreeing modulo $p$ are equal), and is used in the construction of Honda systems, via [`Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_towerHom_map_comp_eq_comp_of_map_L_le`](thm.html#Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_towerHom_map_comp_eq_comp_of_map_L_le).
-- source:
